--- body ---
## Context
On 2026-09-06 `/tmp` (a 12 GB tmpfs, mounted `usrquota`, per-user cap 80 %
set by systemd 259 at login) filled up. Every Bash call in three open Claude
sessions died with EDQUOT from about 12:40, and the machine was rebooted at
16:38. The author purged the filler by hand before rebooting; the shell
history names it: `/tmp/zoteus-wrong*`, `/tmp/zoteus-validation-*`, then
`/tmp/zot*`.

Those names come from the upstream zoteus vitest suite. Test files call
`mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'zoteus-<name>-'))` and never remove the
directory. In the reviewed upstream checkout (`zoteus-fts5/fork`, v1.6.0)
9 test files create such directories and 1 cleans up. In the
`fork-0091` checkout (branch `pr3-droplist`, where Codex added the
`zoteus-validation-*` and `zoteus-wrong-*` tests on 2026-09-01/02) it is 22
files with no cleanup at all.

Measured here, one `npx vitest run` in `fork-0091` under a private `TMPDIR`:

| leftover directories | size |
|---|---|
| 116 | 16 MB |

That is per run. vitest in watch mode re-runs on every save, and Codex and
Claude sessions ran the suite repeatedly from 2026-09-02 to 09-06 on a host
that had not rebooted since 09-02. The run count and the size of the purged
set were not recorded, so the arithmetic from 16 MB per run to a full tmpfs
is not established; the mechanism and the names are.

The temp root is RAM. Filling it is also filling memory, which is why the
host became unresponsive before the quota error even appeared.

## Relevant files
- `~/CNRS/projets/actifs/zoteus-fts5/fork/vitest.config.ts` — no `globalSetup`, no teardown hook
- `~/CNRS/projets/actifs/zoteus-fts5/fork/tests/features/search-backends.test.ts` — `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'zoteus-…'))` with no `rmSync`
- `~/data/projets/zoteus-bench/fork-0091/tests/features/embedder-degradation.test.ts` — the `zoteus-validation-*` / `zoteus-wrong-*` creators
- `bench/smoke_upstream.py` — `TemporaryDirectory(prefix="zoteus-smoke-")`, cleaned on normal exit only
- `bench/acceptance/adapters/zoteus.py` — already redirects `TMPDIR` into the arena; the harness side is fine

## Actions
1. Upstream fix, one file: a vitest `globalSetup` that points `TMPDIR` at a
   fresh per-run directory and removes it in the returned teardown. This
   catches every present and future `tmpdir()` caller without touching the
   22 test files. Per the repo's standing rule the fix ships inside the
   upstream PR being prepared, not as a standalone filing; record it in the
   upstream-PR candidate list.
2. Local mitigation until upstream lands: run the fork suite with `TMPDIR`
   under `~/data` (disk, not RAM), or add a `make test-fork` wrapper that
   does so. Decide which; do not do both.
3. Check `bench/smoke_upstream.py` for the same shape: a killed run leaves
   `zoteus-smoke-*` behind. If the copied index is large, move the scratch
   under the data dir.

## Test
- Run the fork suite once with `TMPDIR` set to an empty directory and assert
  the directory is empty afterwards. Red on the unfixed tree (116 entries),
  green with the teardown.

## Verification
- [x] Positive control recorded: leftover count on the unfixed tree (116, 16 MB, reproduced fresh)
- [x] The teardown test is green on the fixed tree (0 leftover `zoteus-*`, 949/949 unchanged)
- [ ] `ls /tmp | grep -c zoteus-` stays at 0 across a day of sessions — cannot be evidenced in one
      session; the drafted fix has not landed upstream (this raid stopped short of that), so
      `fork-0091`'s own suite is still unfixed and this will read nonzero until it does

## Invariants
- The 949 upstream tests still pass
- The acceptance harness's arena-scoped `TMPDIR` is unchanged

## Exit criteria
- [x] Upstream teardown drafted and listed in the upstream PR candidates
      (`verification/UPSTREAM-PR-0714-TMPDIR-TEARDOWN.md`, `SYNC.md` 2026-09-06 entry;
      staged, not sent — this raid stopped short of upstream by instruction)
- [x] Local mitigation in place: `make test-fork` (`FORK_TEST_TMPDIR ?= $(HOME)/data/fork-test-tmp`)
- [x] `make check` passes (944 passed, 14 skipped)
